A||||11||FieroLisa||Speedo Problem on Mercury Tracer/.||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||01-29-2001||06:24 PM||||This is it, I'm sick of the Tracer!<BR>Ever since I bought it, the speedo has been a litte jumpy, but I've always been able to tell how fast I was going. (Let's say it would jump from 60 to 70 but usually be at 65)<BR>But not even a year later- but with almost 20,000 more miles on the car, this weekend it just gave out. When I was on the highway I had no idea how fast I was going. I'd be blowing by cars when it read at 75. Then someone would pass me while it read 120. Pretty much just jumped all over the place meanwhile making this really annoying whirring noise.  At one point this idiot next to me rolled his window down to ask me if I had a radar detector since he was following me, I said no and asked him how fast we were going (we were neck and neck at this point) He said 60. Mine steadily read 75. Through the entire trip it flipped around like crazy from 65 to 120. It reads fine under 50 mph.<BR>So my question is, what could be the problem and is it worth my time (since I don't have a lot of it to spare) to try to fix it, or just let a shop deal with it?<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||01-30-2001||12:30 AM||||You can try changing the speed sensor which is on the trans.  It might not be the answer.  It would be something i would try.<P>my ford thunderbird would have the speedo just go out off and on, during certain days a few months ago, and now it has stopped doing it for some reason.  It works fine now for 3 months.<P>I dont know if its just me but it seems that ford always has some bugs in the electronics after it gets old with age.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||01-30-2001||12:37 AM||||The best idea is to sell the car..... Speedo problem?? who called me today and said they got crap from a transport driver..who goes 100mph in a tracer anyways<P>Oh yeah ..LISA<P><BR>Not like you pay attention to the speedo<P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||01-30-2001||11:04 AM||||Jonathan, I'd like to answer that. YOU go 100 mph in a tracer ("hey I didn't know it could go that fast!")..ah, but but add to that when the brakes didn't even work right. Good thing I fixed those  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If I sell the tracer- you better start booking lots of plane tickets because I'm not putting 1,000 miles on the GT in one weekend! (And it is 550 miles one way, 7 1/2 hours) <P>The semi-driver can shove it, he probably just wanted an excuse to hit on some girl in a gas station.<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||01-30-2001||03:21 PM||||Call a parts store and ask them if their computer shows it having a Vehicle speed sensor or a speedometer cable.  If it has a cable then you need to replace it. <P>My guess is that you have a speedo cable based on the whirring sound you are hearing from the dash.  Changing it might not be that big of a deal, you would just pull the instrument cluster out and unscrew the old one from that end.<P>The other end either connects directly to the tranny or you might have a two piece cable that goes into a junction right outside the firewall.  They normally break near the end of the cable so it you do have a two piece it should not be hard to tell which one is broken.  <P>If you have a speedo cable at all.  <P>Hope this helps!<P>  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
